.TH GXWI-TEXT-EDITOR 1 2026-10-19 "Peios gxwi-text-editor 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
gxwi-text-editor \- GXWI text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwi-text-editor
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a window on the GXWI desktop with a file of text in it, to read and change.
With no
.I file
the window holds a new one, which is asked a name for when it is first saved.
A
.I file
that is not there is made when it is saved.
.PP
One window holds one file.
The text belongs to the window and not to the browser showing it: what has been typed is the same on every device looking at the session, and is still there when a page is closed and opened again.
Closing the window asks first when there are changes that are not saved.
.PP
Saving writes the file where it is, so that it stays the same file.
Saving under another name makes a new file and never writes over one that is there.
.PP
The file is looked at every two seconds.
If something else changes it and nothing here has changed, it is read again.
If both have changed, the editor asks which is kept.
.PP
Text is UTF-8 with no NUL in it.
The file is opened once and read through that descriptor, with a bounded read that also rejects content growing beyond the limit.
A file that is anything else is not shown, and neither is one of more than 349,525 bytes.
A file whose lines all end with a carriage return and a line feed is written back that way.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
Save under another name.
.SH SECURITY
Reading and saving use the session account's filesystem permissions.
Saving an existing file writes in place and is not an atomic replacement.
Save As creates a new file and refuses an existing destination.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The application session ended normally.
.TP
.B 1
A connection, initialization, or application error prevented normal operation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GXWI_DISPLAY
The display connection supplied by the desktop session.
Launch through the desktop so inherited session descriptors and identity are available.
.TP
.B HOME
The initial or fallback home-directory location.
.SH NOTES
Runs within a GXWI session.
Its parent supplies the session descriptors and identity; launch it through the desktop, or open a file with it from a file explorer.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Peios learn documentation.
